## US-004 – Landing page

### Description

As a visitor,
I want to understand the purpose of Life Goals and see clear login and
registration options,
so that I can decide whether to use the application.

### Business Value

The landing page introduces the product and guides new and returning users
to the correct next action.

### Acceptance Criteria

- The application displays a public landing page before login.
- The main login and sign-up area is displayed prominently.
- The page contains the slogan:
  "Are you ready to make your days more meaningful?"
- The page contains an About Us section.
- The layout works on desktop and mobile devices.
- A returning user can open the login form.
- A new user can open the registration form.

### Priority

High

### MVP

Yes
## US-005 – Goal dashboard

### Description

As an authenticated user,
I want to view, create, and complete my goals,
so that I can manage my progress from one place.

### Acceptance Criteria

- The user can see active goals.
- The user can create a new goal.
- The user can mark an applicable goal or milestone as completed.
- The dashboard displays basic progress information.
- Completed and active goals are visually distinguishable.

### Priority

High

### MVP

Yes
## US-006 – Goal details

### Description

As an authenticated user,
I want to open the details of a goal,
so that I can review its description, milestones, deadline, and progress.

### Acceptance Criteria

- Every goal can be opened from the dashboard.
- The detail page displays the goal title and description.
- It displays the category and goal type.
- It displays the deadline when one exists.
- It displays current and target values for numeric goals.
- It displays milestones or checklist items where applicable.

### Priority

High

### MVP

Yes
## US-008 – Milestone encouragement

### Description

As a user,
I want to receive encouraging feedback after completing a milestone,
so that completing goals feels rewarding and motivating.

### Acceptance Criteria

- Completing a milestone triggers a feedback message.
- The message does not block the user from continuing.
- Feedback may contain practical advice, encouragement, or a light joke.
- The user can choose the preferred feedback style.
- The same message should not be shown repeatedly in a short period.
- The user can disable these messages in settings.

### Priority

Low

### MVP

No